  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 outperforms PCA-2000 by ~3.5 points in the single-profile RNA-only setting (0.520 vs 0.485), establishing scvi_n200 as the best RNA encoder so far. Image-only resnet50 is very weak (0.208), suggesting the RNA pipeline should be optimized before adding a multimodal component. Uncertainty: it is unknown whether multiprofile aggregation adds meaningful signal on top of the scvi_n200 encoder, or whether the single-profile representation already captures the relevant information. This experiment (config_005: scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) tests exactly that question with the simplest aggregation strategy, changing only the profile/aggregation axis from the best RNA-only result (config_004). If avgpool yields a clear gain, it justifies testing transformer aggregation next; if it does not, it suggests multiprofile is not a productive direction and budget should shift to encoder comparison (scgpt) or multimodal fusion. This is the highest-information-per-experiment choice because it resolves a key design axis (profile aggregation) on the strongest known RNA backbone before committing budget to more complex multimodal or aggregation variants."
}

